                    <div id="ppPage" tabindex="-1" role="main">
	<div id="main"><h1>Governor's Executive Orders 2017</h1>
<div id="navcontainer">
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo1">Executive Order 17-01</a></strong><br>Gov. Jay Nixon rescinds Executive Orders <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2007/eo07_010">07-10</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/1986/eo1986_026">86-26</a>, <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/1998/eo98_015">98-15</a>, and <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2005/eo05_040">05-40</a> regarding the Governor's Advisory Council on Physical Fitness and Health and the Missouri State Park Advisory Board. (Jan. 6)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo2">Executive Order 17-02</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens orders state employees of the executive branch of Missouri state government to follow a specified code of conduct. (Jan. 9)<br>- Superseded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2018/eo10">Executive Order 18-10</a><br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo3">Executive Order 17-03</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens orders every state agency to immediately suspend all rulemaking until February 28, 2017, and to complete a review of every regulation under its jurisdiction within the Code of State Regulations by May 31, 2018. (Jan. 10)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo4">Executive Order 17-04</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens establishes the position of Chief Operating Officer to report directly to the Governor and serve as a member of the Governor’s executive team. (Jan. 11)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo5">Executive Order 17-05</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens activates the Missouri State Emergency Operation Center due to forecasted severe winter storms. (Jan. 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo6">Executive Order 17-06</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens declares a State of Emergency, orders the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated, and orders and directs the Adjutant General to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities in response to severe weather that began on January 12, 2017. (Jan. 12)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo7">Executive Order 17-07</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens establishes the Governor's Committee for Simple, Fair and Low Taxes to study tax rates and tax credit programs and recommend comprehensive tax reform legislation. (Jan. 25)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo8">Executive Order 17-08</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated due to severe weather that began on March 6, 2017. (Mar. 7)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo9">Executive Order 17-09</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens establishes parental leave for state employees of the executive branch of Missouri state government and encourages other state officials to adopt comparable policies. (Mar. 13)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo10">Executive Order 17-10</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens designates members of his staff to have supervisory authority over departments, divisions, and agencies of state government. (Apr. 7)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo11">Executive Order 17-11</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens establishes the Boards and Commissions Task Force to recommend comprehensive executive and legislative reform proposals to improve state boards and commissions. (Apr. 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo12">Executive Order 17-12</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens declares a State of Emergency and directs the Missouri State Emergency Operations Plan be activated due to severe weather beginning on April 28, 2017. (Apr. 28)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo13">Executive Order 17-13</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens orders and directs the Adjutant General to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities in response to severe weather that began on April 28, 2017. (Apr. 30)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo14">Executive Order 17-14</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens orders the Director of the Missouri Department of Natural Resources vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period. (May 4)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo15">Executive Order 17-15</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens orders the Director of the Missouri Department of Health and Senior Services vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to severe weather that began on April 28, 2017. (May 8)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo16">Executive Order 17-16</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens orders the Director of the Missouri Department of Revenue vested with full discretionary authority to temporarily waive or suspend statutory or administrative rule or regulation to serve the interests of public health and safety during the period of emergency and subsequent recovery period in response to severe weather that began on April 28, 2017. (May 11)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/Proclamation20170518" aria-label="Proclamation from May 18, 2017"></a></strong><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo17">Executive Order 17-17</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens creates the Missouri State Justice Reinvestment Taskforce to analyze Missouri's corrections system and recommend improvements. (June 28)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2024/eo11">Executive Order 24-11</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo18">Executive Order 17-18</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens directs the Department of Health and Senior Services to create a prescription drug monitoring program. (July 17)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo19">Executive Order 17-19</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens directs the Department of Health and Senior Services, the Department of Mental Health, the Department of Public Safety, the Department of Natural Resources, and the Department of Conservation to identify, train, equip, and assess law enforcement and emergency responder efforts to combat Missouri's Opioid Public Health Crisis. (July 18)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo20">Executive Order 17-20</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens establishes a Board of Inquiry to review evidence and provide a recommendation on the death sentence for inmate Marcellus Williams. A stay of execution is ordered until the Governor makes a final determination. (Aug. 22)<br>- Rescinded by <a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2023/eo6">Executive Order 23-06</a></p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo21">Executive Order 17-21</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens orders and directs the Adjutant General to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities in anticipation of unrest in the St. Louis region. (Sep. 14)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo22">Executive Order 17-22</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens implements the Emergency Mutual Assistance Compact (EMAC) with the Virgin Islands, directs the State Emergency Management Agency to activate the EMAC plan, and orders the Adjutant General to call into active service any state militia deemed necessary to support civilian authorities in response to Hurricane Maria. (Sep. 20)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo23">Executive Order 17-23</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens orders state offices to be closed on Friday, November 24, 2017. (Nov. 1)</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.sos.mo.gov/library/reference/orders/2017/eo24">Executive Order 17-24</a></strong><br>Gov. Eric Greitens designates members of his staff to have supervisory authority over departments, divisions, and agencies of state government. (Nov. 17)</p>
</div>
<p>
